---@alias gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.OccurrenceList gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.Occurrence[]

---This resource represents a long-running operation that is the result of a network API call.
---@class gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.Operation
---@field metadata? gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.DocumentMap Service-specific metadata associated with the operation. It typically contains progress information and common metadata such as create time. Some services might not provide such metadata. Any method that returns a long-running operation should document the metadata type, if any.
---@field response? gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.DocumentMap The normal, successful response of the operation. If the original method returns no data on success, such as `Delete`, the response is `google.protobuf.Empty`. If the original method is standard `Get`/`Create`/`Update`, the response should be the resource. For other methods, the response should have the type `XxxResponse`, where `Xxx` is the original method name. For example, if the original method name is `TakeSnapshot()`, the inferred response type is `TakeSnapshotResponse`.
---@field error? gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.Status The error result of the operation in case of failure or cancellation.
---@field name? string The server-assigned name, which is only unique within the same service that originally returns it. If you use the default HTTP mapping, the `name` should be a resource name ending with `operations/{unique_id}`.
---@field done? boolean If the value is `false`, it means the operation is still in progress. If `true`, the operation is completed, and either `error` or `response` is available.

---@alias gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.OperationList gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.Operation[]

---@class gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.PackageData
---@field package? string The package being analysed for vulnerabilities
---@field unused? string
---@field layerDetails? gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.LayerDetails Deprecated: Layer details are captured per file location in FileLocation.layer_details. Top-level layer details is not persisted.
---@field hashDigest? string HashDigest stores the SHA512 hash digest of the jar file if the package is of type Maven. This field will be unset for non Maven packages.
---@field binarySourceInfo? gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.BinarySourceInfoList A bundle containing the binary and source information.
---@field cpeUri? string The cpe_uri in [cpe format] (https://cpe.mitre.org/specification/) in which the vulnerability may manifest. Examples include distro or storage location for vulnerable jar.
---@field licenses? gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.StringList Deprecated: Top-level licenses is not persisted in the legacy Packages table. Licenses are captured in BinarySourceInfo or PackagesV2.
---@field packageType? gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.PackageDataPackageTypeEnum|string The type of package: os, maven, go, etc.
