---@field name? string Required only when version kind is NORMAL. The main part of the version name.
---@field fullName? string Human readable version string. This string is of the form :- and is only set when kind is NORMAL.
---@field inclusive? boolean Whether this version is specifying part of an inclusive range. Grafeas does not have the capability to specify version ranges; instead we have fields that specify start version and end versions. At times this is insufficient - we also need to specify whether the version is included in the range or is excluded from the range. This boolean is expected to be set to true when the version is included in a range.
---@field epoch? number Used to correct mistakes in the version numbering scheme.
---@field kind? gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.VersionKindEnum Required. Distinguishes between sentinel MIN/MAX versions and normal versions.
---@field revision? string The iteration of the package build from the above version.

---@alias gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.VersionKindEnum "VERSION_KIND_UNSPECIFIED"|"NORMAL"|"MINIMUM"|"MAXIMUM"

---VexAssessment provides all publisher provided Vex information that is related to this vulnerability.
---@class gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.VexAssessment
---@field impacts? gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.StringList Contains information about the impact of this vulnerability, this will change with time.
---@field justification? gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.Justification Justification provides the justification when the state of the assessment if NOT_AFFECTED.
---@field remediations? gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.RemediationList Specifies details on how to handle (and presumably, fix) a vulnerability.
---@field state? gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.VexAssessmentStateEnum Provides the state of this Vulnerability assessment.
---@field relatedUris? gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.RelatedUrlList Holds a list of references associated with this vulnerability item and assessment.
---@field noteName? string The VulnerabilityAssessment note from which this VexAssessment was generated. This will be of the form: `projects/[PROJECT_ID]/notes/[NOTE_ID]`.
---@field vulnerabilityId? string The vulnerability identifier for this Assessment. Will hold one of common identifiers e.g. CVE, GHSA etc.
---@field cve? string Holds the MITRE standard Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures (CVE) tracking number for the vulnerability. Deprecated: Use vulnerability_id instead to denote CVEs.

---@alias gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.VexAssessmentStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"AFFECTED"|"NOT_AFFECTED"|"FIXED"|"UNDER_INVESTIGATION"

---An occurrence of a severity vulnerability on a resource.
---@class gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.VulnerabilityOccurrence
---@field type? string The type of package; whether native or non native (e.g., ruby gems, node.js packages, etc.).
---@field cvssScore? number Output only. The CVSS score of this vulnerability. CVSS score is on a scale of 0 - 10 where 0 indicates low severity and 10 indicates high severity.
---@field exploitability? gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.Exploitability Output only. Rollup of exploitability across all PackageIssues in this occurrence.
---@field cvssV4? gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.CVSS The cvss v4 score for the vulnerability.
---@field relatedUrls? gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.RelatedUrlList Output only. URLs related to this vulnerability.
---@field longDescription? string Output only. A detailed description of this vulnerability.
---@field severity? gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.VulnerabilityOccurrenceSeverityEnum Output only. The note provider assigned severity of this vulnerability.
---@field effectiveSeverity? gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.VulnerabilityOccurrenceEffectiveSeverityEnum The distro assigned severity for this vulnerability when it is available, otherwise this is the note provider assigned severity. When there are multiple PackageIssues for this vulnerability, they can have different effective severities because some might be provided by the distro while others are provided by the language ecosystem for a language pack. For this reason, it is advised to use the effective severity on the PackageIssue level. In the case where multiple PackageIssues have differing effective severities, this field should be the highest severity for any of the PackageIssues.
---@field risk? gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.Risk Risk information about the vulnerability, such as CISA, EPSS, etc.
---@field cvssV2? gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.CVSS The cvss v2 score for the vulnerability.
---@field shortDescription? string Output only. A one sentence description of this vulnerability.
---@field packageIssue? gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.PackageIssueList Required. The set of affected locations and their fixes (if available) within the associated resource.
---@field fixAvailable? boolean Output only. Whether at least one of the affected packages has a fix available.
---@field extraDetails? string Occurrence-specific extra details about the vulnerability.
---@field vexAssessment? gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.VexAssessment
---@field cvssVersion? gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.VulnerabilityOccurrenceCvssVersionEnum Output only. CVSS version used to populate cvss_score and severity.
---@field cvssv3? gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.CVSS The cvss v3 score for the vulnerability.

---@alias gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.VulnerabilityOccurrenceCvssVersionEnum "CVSS_VERSION_UNSPECIFIED"|"CVSS_VERSION_2"|"CVSS_VERSION_3"|"CVSS_VERSION_4"

---@alias gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.VulnerabilityOccurrenceEffectiveSeverityEnum "SEVERITY_UNSPECIFIED"|"MINIMAL"|"LOW"|"MEDIUM"|"HIGH"|"CRITICAL"

---@alias gcp.ondemandscanning_v1.VulnerabilityOccurrenceSeverityEnum "SEVERITY_UNSPECIFIED"|"MINIMAL"|"LOW"|"MEDIUM"|"HIGH"|"CRITICAL"

